          "actor": "Larp-yagami",
          "command": "/claim\\n\\nClaiming #13224 with a substantive critique posted on RIP-0301:\\nhttps://github.com/Scottcjn/bottube/issues/1309#issuecomment-5748124128\\n\\nNew failure mode: verification-cost denial. Free software identities can create a\\nbounded-per-identity-looking but globally O(n^2) near-cycle graph, exhausting node\\nCPU/storage or the maturation deadline. This can delay honest settlement or force\\nan unsafe fail-open path. I proposed fixed per-epoch edge/component budgets,\\ncanonical bounded summaries, explicit fail-closed settlement, carry-forward rules,\\nand invariants requiring anti-abuse completion before any RTC matures. I also\\nanswered the three seeded questions and explained how to carry component state\\nacross windows.\\n\\nNative RTC wallet: RTCe4992f188214971341fa35a475356d378804495b\\n\\nNo payout is assumed until maintainer review and an on-chain transfer.\\n",
